al","la":-18.133224,"lo":178.425886,"d":779,"h":"Mo-Th 08:00-16:30; Fr 08:00-16:00"},{"n":"786 Hypermart","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":-18.13882,"lo":178.431312,"d":783},{"n":"Suva Private Hospital Phamarcy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":-18.13679,"lo":178.432323,"d":949},{"n":"Suva Private Hospital","g":"essentials","k":"hospital","la":-18.136869,"lo":178.432485,"d":961},{"n":"CWM HOSPITAL (Maternity Unit)","g":"essentials","k":"hospital","la":-18.13416,"lo":178.433299,"d":1177},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":-18.133868,"lo":178.433272,"d":1193},{"n":"Reserve Bank of Fiji","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-18.1396,"lo":178.4251,"d":124,"ds":"The Reserve Bank of Fiji (RBF; Fijian: Maroroi Baqe ni Viti, Fiji Hindi: फिजी रिजर्व बैंक) is the central bank of the Pacific island country of Fiji. Its responsibilities include the issue of currency, control of the money supply, currency exchange, monetary stability, promotion of sound finances, and fostering economic development.","wpu":"Reserve Bank of Fiji","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mercury_House_Suva_MatthiasSuessen-7834.jpg/960px-Mercury_House_Suva_MatthiasSuessen-7834.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Diocese of Polynesia","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-18.142392,"lo":178.424469,"d":270,"ds":"The Diocese of Polynesia, or the Tikanga Pasefika serves Anglicans in Fiji, Tonga, Samoa, Aotearoa New Zealand and the Cook Islands, within the Anglican Church in Aotearoa, New Zealand and Polynesia. The diocese's first bishop was consecrated in 1908. The diocese's cathedral is Holy Trinity Cathedral in Suva, Fiji.","wpu":"Diocese of Polynesia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Guard_Suva_MatthiasSuessen-8368.jpg/960px-Guard_Suva_MatthiasSuessen-8368.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Albert Park (Suva)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-18.1473,"lo":178.4249,"d":817,"ds":"Albert Park is located in Suva, the capital of Fiji. It was named after Prince Albert, the Consort of Queen Victoria of Great Britain, to whom the country was ceded in 1874. Albert Park can hold two rugby matches at one time.","wpu":"Albert Park (Suva)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/USP_Bure_MatthiasSuessen-8729.jpg/960px-USP_Bure_MatthiasSuessen-8729.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"WG Friendship Plaza Suva","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-18.146389,"lo":178.430833,"d":1012,"ds":"The WG Friendship Plaza Suva is a high-rise mixed-use skyscraper under construction in Suva, Fiji, currently serving as the tallest building in the country, as well as the tallest building in Oceania outside Australia and New Zealand. The tower was topped out in 2021 and is 112 meters (367 ft) tall, being divided into 28 floors. The official opening was expected to take place in the second half of 2024.","wpu":"WG Friendship Plaza Suva","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/WG_Plaza_Tower_Suva_2023.jpg/960px-WG_Plaza_Tower_Suva_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sacred Heart Cathedral, Suva","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-18.1416,"lo":178.442,"d":1910,"ds":"The Sacred Heart Cathedral or simply Cathedral of Suva, is the main ecclesiastical building of the Roman Catholic Church in the island nation of Fiji, and is located on Pratt Street in the City of Suva, Fiji's capital. Suva Cathedral was built in 1902 with sandstone brought from quarries near Sydney, Australia. Its architecture is inspired by the churches of Rome in Italy.","wpu":"Sacred Heart Cathedral, Suva","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Sacred_Heart_Cathedral%2C_Suva_Fiji_July_2014.jpg/960px-Sacred_Heart_Cathedral%2C_Suva_Fiji_July_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Suva Fiji Temple","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-18.119722,"lo":178.438556,"d":2729,"ds":"The Suva Fiji Temple is the 91st operating temple of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (LDS Church). The intent to build the temple was announced on 5 April 1998, by church president Gordon B. Hinckley during the church's general conference. The temple is the first to be built in Fiji.","wpu":"Suva Fiji Temple","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Suva_Fiji_Temple_by_bhaskarroo_cropped.jpg/960px-Suva_Fiji_Temple_by_bhaskarroo_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Suva (Fijian: [ˈsuβa] SOO-vuh, Fiji Hindi: सुवा) is the capital and most populous settlement of Fiji. It is the centre of Fiji's largest metropolitan area and serves as its major port. The city is on the southeast coast of the island of Viti Levu, in Rewa Province, Central Division.","wpu":"Suva","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Suva%2C_Fiji_77.jpg/960px-Suva%2C_Fiji_77.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}